      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0141",
      "sequence": 153,
      "meaning": "Śiva asks the mountain’s daughter to hear another, elaborately wondrous cause for the unborn, attributeless, formless Brahman becoming king in Ayodhyā. It concerns the Lord whom she once saw wandering the forest with his brother in an ascetic guise and whose deeds left Satī bewildered—hearing them will cure the lingering shadow of that confusion. Śiva will relate the incarnation’s entire play as far as his understanding permits. Hearing this, Umā smiles with loving reserve, and Vṛṣaketu begins describing the reason for that descent. The delightful Rāma-story destroys the impurity of the dark age and creates auspiciousness; the sage should listen attentively.",
