      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0142",
      "sequence": 154,
      "meaning": "Svāyambhuva Manu and Śatarūpā, from whom the matchless human race arose, were a couple of exemplary righteousness whose conduct the Vedas still celebrate. Their elder son Uttānapāda fathered the devotee Dhruva; the younger, Priyavrata, is praised by Vedas and Purāṇas. Their daughter Devahūti became Kardama’s beloved wife, and in her womb the merciful primal Lord appeared as Kapila and expounded Sāṅkhya with expert analysis of reality. Manu ruled long and obeyed the Lord’s command in every way, but old age arrived while he still lacked detachment from objects. He grieved that life had passed without devotion to Hari.",
