      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0143",
      "sequence": 155,
      "meaning": "Manu forcibly gives the kingdom to his son and leaves with his wife for the forest. They go joyfully to renowned, holy Naimiṣa, giver of accomplishment to seekers and home to communities of perfected sages; on the road the wise pair seem knowledge and devotion embodied. At the Dhenu river they bathe in pure water and are welcomed as a royal sage and pillar of dharma. The sages reverently take them to every lovely holy place. Emaciated and dressed in ascetic cloth, the couple daily hear Purāṇas in saintly company and lovingly repeat the twelve-syllable mantra, their minds fixed deeply on Vāsudeva’s lotus feet.",
