    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0144",
      "sequence": 156,
      "meaning": "Manu and Śatarūpā eat vegetables, fruits and roots and remember Brahman, existence-consciousness-bliss. They then undertake austerity for Hari, first living on water and abandoning roots and fruits. Their constant longing is to behold with their own eyes the supreme Lord whom seekers of ultimate truth contemplate as attributeless, indivisible, infinite and beginningless; whom the Vedas define by ‘not this, not this’; who is self-blissful, unconditioned and incomparable; and from whose portions Śiva, Brahmā and Viṣṇu arise. Yet that very Lord submits to servants and assumes playful bodies for devotees. Trusting the Vedic word, they hope their desire will be fulfilled. Six thousand years pass on water, then seven thousand sustained by air.",
