    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0145",
      "sequence": 157,
      "meaning": "For ten thousand further years the couple abandon even air and remain standing on one foot, reduced to skeletons but without the slightest mental pain. Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Śiva repeatedly approach, amazed by their boundless austerity, and tempt them in many ways to request a boon, but the steadfast pair cannot be moved. The omniscient Lord recognizes king and queen as wholly single-minded servants. A profound, nectar-filled voice sounds from the sky: ‘Ask, ask a boon.’ Its beautiful, life-restoring sound enters their ears, and their bodies at once become robust and lovely as if they had just left the palace. Thrilled and overflowing with love, Manu bows prostrate and speaks.",
